-n for number of character's to read

-s for nonechoed reading (ie password)

-p for prompting

-t timeout 

-d delimiter


read -n 2 var

The above line read's two character to the variable 'var'

read -p 'Enter name:' var

The above line display's the prompt and read's the value into the variable'var'

read -s var

The above line is used to read the password in nonechoed 

read -t 2 var

The above line is used to character or text that is been entered in 2 second's of duration

read -d ":" var

The above line is used to end the read after the delimiter


